ry first checks client and transaction conventions, which blocks the exact bulk contract, with the recorded atomic 500-ID API default if none is found. Discovery leads [hints, not verified facts]: repository owners, support leads, operations team, deployment configuration, internal team channels and documentation, relay consumers, and any private service repositories may clarify actor trust, weekly boundaries, batching and prior conventions; no specific private locator is known, and any sensitive locator belongs only in an authorized private store, never KNOWLEDGE/. Interaction and state [fact/default]: agents and API clients act through HTTP, requesters receive relay messages, and operators inspect outbox and audit; X-Actor is unverified and defaults to system, shared state is process-owned with optional file persistence, and no session or per-person visibility controls are established. Discovery must establish deployment identity, access controls, multi-process use and consumer expectations before any stronger privacy or concurrency claim; the default preserves the current internal single-process model and rules out assuming authenticated identities or shared multi-process coordination. Delivery [fact]: the named repository is the authorized target; the result becomes visible in the isolated checkout at final return and in a deployed service only after release, for which no target or access has been established."
